  "body_html": "<h1>Von Neumann Minimax Theorem</h1>\n<p>For every finite real matrix game $A$, there exist mixed strategies\n$x^* \\in \\Delta(I)$ and $y^* \\in \\Delta(J)$ and a real number $v$ such that\n$$\n  x^* A y \\ge v \\quad \\text{for all } y \\in \\Delta(J),\n$$\nand\n$$\n  x A y^* \\le v \\quad \\text{for all } x \\in \\Delta(I).\n$$\nEquivalently, the mixed extension has a value\n$$\n  v=\\max_{x \\in \\Delta(I)}\\min_{y \\in \\Delta(J)} xAy\n   =\\min_{y \\in \\Delta(J)}\\max_{x \\in \\Delta(I)} xAy.\n$$</p>\n<h2>References</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>[MFoGT, Theorem 2.3.1] Laraki, Renault, and Sorin, <em>Mathematical Foundations of Game Theory</em>, <code>references/MechDesign.pdf</code>. Von Neumann minimax theorem for finite matrix games.</li>\n</ul>",
  "proof_html": null,
